[SIZE="4"][B]About[/B][/SIZE]

This is an unofficial [B]LineageOS 11 (Android 4.4.4 KitKat)[/B] build for the [B]LG G2 Mini LTE D625[/B] (codename [B]g2mv[/B]). It is the first custom ROM for this model, which uses an [B]NVIDIA Tegra 4i[/B] instead of a Snapdragon, so nothing from the D620/D618 ports applies to it.

The kernel is built from LG's GPL source with fixes for this ROM (backlight, proximity, flash, KnockON). Proprietary files come from stock firmware D62510c. Every result listed below was checked on real hardware.

[COLOR="Red"][B]Only for the Tegra 4i D625. It will not boot on the Snapdragon G2 Mini models (D620, D618...).[/B][/COLOR]

[COLOR="Red"][B]Requires the patched bootloader and TWRP:[/B][/COLOR]
[LIST=1]
[*][URL="PUT_BOOTLOADER_GUIDE_URL_HERE"][GUIDE] How To Unlock the Bootloader LG G2 Mini LTE D625 (Tegra 4i)[/URL]
[*][URL="PUT_TWRP_THREAD_URL_HERE"][RECOVERY][UNOFFICIAL] TWRP 3.1.1-1 for LG G2 Mini LTE D625[/URL]
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Device specs[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*]Device: LG G2 Mini LTE (LG-D625), codename g2mv
[*]Android version: 4.4.4 KitKat (LineageOS 11, the LineageOS-maintained cm-11.0 branch with later security patches)
[*]Kernel: Linux 3.4.65, compiled from source (pda_android_defconfig)
[*]SoC: NVIDIA Tegra 4i (T148), quad-core ARM Cortex-A9 up to 1.73 GHz
[*]GPU: NVIDIA ULP GeForce (OpenGL ES 2.0), up to 595 MHz
[*]RAM: 1 GB
[*]Display: 4.7 inch, 540x960, 60 Hz
[*]Modem: NVIDIA Icera (2G/3G)
[*]Base firmware: D62510c (Android 4.4.2)
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Current status: Beta[/B][/SIZE]

[COLOR="Red"][B]Read the known issues before flashing.[/B][/COLOR] This is a first public build. Calls, data, Wi-Fi and Bluetooth work, but some items below are still being fixed.

[SIZE="4"][B]What's working:[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Boot:[/B] boots to the launcher; screen ready about 13 s after the kernel starts on a normal boot.
[*][B]Display and HW acceleration:[/B] NVIDIA GLES driver and hwcomposer overlays. The RT8542 backlight is controlled by the ROM. Auto-brightness works.
[*][B]Touch:[/B] multitouch, with an on-screen navigation bar.
[*][B]KnockON (double tap to wake):[/B] toggle in Settings > Display. It wakes from deep sleep and is blocked when the proximity sensor is covered (pocket).
[*][B]Calls and SIM:[/B] Icera modem, voice calls and HSPA data (tested on Claro Peru). The in-call proximity sensor turns the screen off at your ear.
[*][B]Wi-Fi:[/B] Broadcom bcmdhd, WPA2.
[*][B]Bluetooth:[/B] BCM4334, scan and pairing.
[*][B]Audio:[/B] speaker, earpiece, headset and microphone, using the stock NVIDIA audio HAL.
[*][B]Camera:[/B] photos, flash, video recording and playback with NVIDIA hardware codecs.
[*][B]Torch:[/B] works from the Torch app and as video light. The LED switches off when the camera closes.
[*][B]Sensors:[/B] accelerometer, magnetometer, proximity and light.
[*][B]Vibrator:[/B] max77660 haptics.
[*][B]Deep sleep:[/B] Tegra LP0 suspend. The modem wakes the phone for calls and SMS.
[*][B]Offline charging:[/B] stock LG charge animation when the phone is off.
[*][B]IR blaster:[/B] stock LG QuickRemote and UEI QuickSet (TV codes from the built-in database).
[*][B]GPS:[/B] the stack and AGPS start, but see the known issues.
[*][B]NVIDIA power management:[/B] powerservice and ussrd run as on stock, with the interactive CPU governor.
[*][B]Root:[/B] built-in superuser (Settings > Developer options > Root access).
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Known issues:[/B][/SIZE]
[LIST]
[*][B]Recorded video looks pixelated.[/B] The NVIDIA H.264 encoder ignores the requested bitrate and writes about 180 kbps instead of 4 Mbps. Photos are not affected. Under investigation.
[*][B]"Media server died" after recording video.[/B] The main cause, a use-after-free in the cm-11.0 OMX node teardown (from its CVE-2017-13154 backport), was found and a fix is included in this build. If you still see camera or media restarts, please report them with a logcat.
[*][B]Incoming calls while the phone sleeps can be missed in weak coverage.[/B] In poor signal the modem sometimes loses network registration while the CPU is in deep sleep, and the network never pages it. With good signal, calls come in from deep sleep. Still being compared with the stock ROM.
[*][B]No deep sleep for about 5 minutes after each boot.[/B] The GPS daemon holds a wakelock while it initializes. After that, sleep works normally.
[*][B]LTE (4G):[/B] enabled (preferred network LTE/WCDMA/GSM, selectable in Settings), but a 4G connection is not confirmed yet. There is no LTE coverage at the test location: the LG stock ROM also stays on 3G (HSPA+) there. If you have 4G coverage, please report whether you get LTE.
[*][B]GPS:[/B] an outdoor satellite fix is not confirmed yet (0 satellites indoors).
[*][B]NFC:[/B] the controller polls, but reading a tag is not field-tested. The NFC service also restarts on every screen on/off.
[*][B]IR blaster:[/B] only the stock QuickRemote app works. Third-party IR apps (Android ConsumerIr API) do not, and the brand list comes from QuickSet's limited database.
[/LIST]

